map of the yupiter repository
=============================

yupiter is a freestanding C library for Linux on aarch64 and x86_64.
No host C library is used: it supplies its own entry point, syscall
layer and formatting engine.  The interface is ISO C17; the
implementation is ISO C++23, built freestanding.


Top-level entries
-----------------

.github/     CI workflows, dependency updates, code scanning.
python/      PyO3/maturin binding.  Not part of the library build.
             See docs/python-binding.
assembly/    Freestanding entry point and syscall trampolines.
io/          Streams, formatting and the Linux syscall layer (C++23).
mem/         Allocator (C++23).
include/     Public headers and internal headers shared with tests.
etc/         Templates for installed package metadata.
mk/          Makefile modules.
docs/        This directory.
test/        C tests plus a C++ compatibility test.
build/       Generated build tree (ignored, removed by make clean).


Top-level files
---------------

AUTHORS         Maintainers.
ChangeLog       Points to Git for detailed history.
LICENSE         License overview and how to choose.
LICENSES/       Full license texts.
Makefile        Top-level build.
configure       POSIX script that detects the target, writes config.mk.
NEWS            Release notes, newest first.
README          Project overview.


